1
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:50,950
Your Grace, if you'd like to sit, I'm sure that.

2
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:53,020
We've been here since midday.

3
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:05,160
Easterners have a difference sense of time, I've often found.

4
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:09,230
Once, I was waiting for Salladhor Saan here in Braavos.

5
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:13,520
Together, we were going to run three shiploads of the finest.

6
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,780
Welcome to the Iron Bank.

7
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:46,960
Please, sit.

8
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:12,050
What can we do for you, Lord Stannis?

9
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,610
This is Stannis of the House Baratheon,

10
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,460
King of the Andals and the First Men,

11
00:04:16,470 --> 00:04:19,290
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms and Protector of the Realm.

12
00:04:23,310 --> 00:04:25,240
The Iron Throne is currently occupied

13
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:27,190
by Tommen of the House Baratheon,

14
00:04:27,190 --> 00:04:29,030
King of the Andals and the First Men,

15
00:04:29,030 --> 00:04:32,020
Lord of the Seven Kingdoms and Protector of the Realm.

16
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:34,700
He shares no blood with me.

17
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:38,130
He is a bastard born of incest.

18
00:04:38,130 --> 00:04:39,920
As was his brother before him.

19
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,830
Yes, we have heard this story.

20
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:45,650
It's not a story. It's the truth.

21
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:48,540
The king's grandfather tells a different story.

22
00:04:49,410 --> 00:04:51,050
A story about a jealous uncle

23
00:04:51,050 --> 00:04:53,780
whose attempts to usurp the throne from the rightful king

24
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:58,550
cost the Seven Kingdoms dearly in blood and gold.

25
00:04:58,550 --> 00:05:00,150
Gold you loaned him.

26
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:04,650
And you feel your blood gives you a claim on our gold?

27
00:05:05,110 --> 00:05:07,140
More than any man living.

28
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:09,880
Across the Narrow Sea, your books are filled

29
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:13,280
with words like "usurper" and "madman"

30
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:15,560
and "blood right."

31
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:19,080
Here, our books are filled with numbers.

32
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:21,130
We prefer the stories they tell.

33
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:23,060
More plain.

34
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:26,430
Less open to interpretation.

35
00:05:29,050 --> 00:05:31,790
How many fighting men remain loyal to you?

36
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,420
4,000.

37
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:35,110
And how many ships do you have?

38
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:37,460
The ones still afloat, Ser Davos,

39
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:39,810
not at the bottom of Blackwater Bay.

40
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,110
32.

41
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:45,200
And how much wheat and barley and beef

42
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,500
and pork do you produce on Dragonstone

43
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:52,380
to feed your 4,000 men on your 32 ships?

44
00:05:54,670 --> 00:05:55,910
None.

45
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:59,070
You can see why these numbers seem unlikely to add up

46
00:05:59,070 --> 00:06:02,430
to a happy ending from our perspective.

47
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:08,070
I'm afraid we must respectfully decline your request.

48
00:06:09,690 --> 00:06:12,260
But we thank you for paying us the honor of your visit.

49
00:06:21,570 --> 00:06:22,410
My lord.

50
00:06:22,410 --> 00:06:25,480
I'm not a lord, Ser Davos Seaworth.

51
00:06:25,610 --> 00:06:27,630
You would not be either here.

52
00:06:27,650 --> 00:06:29,190
In Braavos,

53
00:06:29,630 --> 00:06:32,480
thieves are not rewarded with titles.

54
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:34,220
Well, strictly speaking, I didn't do the thieving.

55
00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:35,850
That would be the pirates.

56
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:38,960
I just moved what they stole from one place to another.

57
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:44,260
This is the payment that was demanded by King Stannis for my crimes.

58
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:46,590
I consider it an honest accounting.

59
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:48,940
He's an honest man and he's your best chance

60
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:51,330
to get back the money you've sunk into Westeros.

61
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:54,420
Which is a lot, I imagine. Wars are expensive.

62
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:55,590
The war is over.

63
00:06:55,590 --> 00:06:58,420
As long as Stannis lives, the war is not over.

64
00:06:58,620 --> 00:07:00,540
Who's the real power in King's Landing?

65
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:02,730
-Ser Davos.  -Humor me.

66
00:07:03,110 --> 00:07:06,210
-Tywin Lannister.  -How old is Tywin Lannister?

67
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:09,260
-67.  -67. And when he dies, who's in command?

68
00:07:10,190 --> 00:07:13,300
A half-grown boy, the product of incest?

69
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:16,750
Cersei Lannister, a queen whose people despise her?

70
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:19,340
Jaime Lannister, a man best known for killing the king

71
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:21,590
he was sworn to protect?

72
00:07:22,090 --> 00:07:25,610
When Tywin's gone, who do you back?

73
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:28,010
That is a problem for another time.

74
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:30,070
Begging your pardon, I think it's a problem for now.

75
00:07:31,350 --> 00:07:34,690
There's only one reliable leader left in Westeros.

76
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,320
Stannis.

77
00:07:36,470 --> 00:07:38,090
He's got the birthright.

78
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:39,700
He's in his prime.

79
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:42,220
He's a tried and tested battle commander.

80
00:07:42,230 --> 00:07:44,410
And he doesn't just talk about paying people back,

81
00:07:44,410 --> 00:07:45,690
he does it.

82
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:52,530
The lookout sees a pirate ship sailing their way.

83
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:54,700
The captain shouts to his first mate,

84
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:56,800
"Bring me my red shirt."

85
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:59,660
The first mate brings the red shirt and the captain puts it on.

86
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:01,350
And when the pirates try to board,

87
00:08:01,350 --> 00:08:04,130
the brave captain leads his men to victory.

88
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:07,360
A few days later, the lookout screams,

89
00:08:07,370 --> 00:08:09,230
"Two pirate ships!"

90
00:08:09,450 --> 00:08:13,320
The crew is shivering like scared mice.

91
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:15,290
But the courageous captain hollers,

92
00:08:15,290 --> 00:08:16,990
"Bring me my red shirt!"

93
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:19,300
After the battle, the first mate asks,

94
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:23,070
"Captain, why do you call for your red shirt before battle?"

95
00:08:23,070 --> 00:08:24,630
The captain replies,

96
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:28,310
"So that if I am stabbed, you will not see me bleed."

97
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,760
The next morning the lookout screams,

98
00:08:31,270 --> 00:08:33,250
"10 pirate ships!

99
00:08:33,290 --> 00:08:34,950
We are surrounded!"

100
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,900
The crew goes silent.

101
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:40,620
They all look to their brave captain,

102
00:08:40,630 --> 00:08:42,690
waiting for his usual command.

103
00:08:42,690 --> 00:08:44,910
Calm as ever, the captain bellows.

104
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:46,880
"Bring me my brown pants!"

105
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:53,340
You think they ever met a pirate who didn't tell them that joke?

106
00:08:54,650 --> 00:08:55,820
Davos.

107
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:59,180
I heard you were rotting in a dungeon in Dragonstone.

108
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,670
Only half rotted.

109
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:06,560
Join us, my friend. Join us.

110
00:09:06,870 --> 00:09:08,820
This is Lhara.

111
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:11,120
-And this is.  -I am Lhara.

112
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:16,900
She's an artist, this one, truly.

113
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:20,160
No time, I'm afraid. We sail at sunrise.

114
00:09:20,570 --> 00:09:21,620
We?

115
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:23,590
You, me, we.

116
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:29,280
Once I thought this man loved me,

117
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:32,560
now I know he despises me.

118
00:09:33,190 --> 00:09:37,740
He wants to see me die poor and alone on some cold.

119
00:09:47,430 --> 00:09:48,930
You won't be alone.

120
00:09:49,230 --> 00:09:50,760
And you won't be poor.

121
00:09:58,330 --> 00:10:01,090
There's a chest of the good stuff left back at your house.

122
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,270
I gave it to your wife.

123
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:08,170
You're not my friend, my friend.

124
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:12,220
I'll see you at sunrise.

125
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,350
"I give you until the full moon

126
00:10:17,350 --> 00:10:20,930
to order all ironborn scum out of the North

127
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:24,320
and back to those shit-stained rocks you call home.

128
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:26,710
On the first night of the full moon,

129
00:10:26,710 --> 00:10:29,590
I will hunt down every islander still on our lands

130
00:10:29,590 --> 00:10:31,280
and flay them living,

131
00:10:31,470 --> 00:10:34,210
the way I flayed the 20 ironborn scum

132
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:35,840
I found at Winterfell.

133
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,620
In the box you'll find a special gift.

134
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:42,650
Theon's favorite toy.

135
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:46,160
He cried when I took it away from him.

136
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:50,180
Leave the North now or more boxes will follow

137
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:51,950
with more Theon.

138
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:54,870
Signed Ramsay Snow,

139
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:58,140
natural born son of Roose Bolton,

140
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,280
Lord of the Dreadfort

141
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:02,690
and Warden of the North."

142
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,470
Yes!

143
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:07,260
They skinned our countrymen

144
00:11:07,410 --> 00:11:10,210
and they mutilated my brother,

145
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,870
your prince.

146
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,360
Your prince.

147
00:11:14,870 --> 00:11:17,330
Everything they've done to him,

148
00:11:17,330 --> 00:11:19,380
they've also done to you.

149
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:20,960
Yes! Yes!

150
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:24,760
As long as they can hurt our prince with impunity,

151
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:28,550
the word ironborn means nothing.

152
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:53,880
Go left.

153
00:12:03,630 --> 00:12:05,640
-Theon Greyjoy.  -I don't know.

154
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:07,070
I'm here for Theon Greyjoy.

155
00:12:07,070 --> 00:12:08,710
Take me to the dungeons.

156
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,250
He's not in the dungeons.

157
00:12:34,890 --> 00:12:36,920
-Last cage on the right.  -Thank you.

158
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:41,850
This way!

159
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,340
We're going home.

160
00:12:58,960 --> 00:12:59,850
No!

161
00:13:03,450 --> 00:13:06,940
It's all right. It's me, Yara.

162
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,580
You can't trick me.

163
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:11,080
Tell him. Tell him, you couldn't trick me.

164
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:13,330
I'm not tricking you, Theon. I'm saving you.

165
00:13:13,330 --> 00:13:14,890
Not Theon! Reek!

166
00:13:14,890 --> 00:13:16,400
Reek! My name is Reek!

167
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:17,710
If they catch us in here, we're trapped.

168
00:13:17,710 --> 00:13:18,960
Help me with him.

169
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,130
No, you can't!

170
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,750
-You can't!  -You're Theon Greyjoy.

171
00:13:24,370 --> 00:13:28,000
No, I don't believe her! I know who I am!

172
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,670
I'm Reek! Reek! Loyal Reek!

173
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:33,540
Good Reek! I've always been Reek!

174
00:13:44,110 --> 00:13:47,050
This is turning into a lovely evening.

175
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,930
I'm Reek! Loyal Reek!

176
00:14:15,270 --> 00:14:16,240
Theon!

177
00:14:29,430 --> 00:14:32,580
Give me my brother and no more of your men will die.

178
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,940
You've got bigger balls than he ever did.

179
00:14:37,870 --> 00:14:41,340
But with those big balls of yours,

180
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:48,450
how fast can you run?

181
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,950
Make for the ship, now.

182
00:15:01,950 --> 00:15:02,990
But your brother.

183
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,270
My brother is dead.

184
00:15:13,570 --> 00:15:15,100
I have a treat for you.

185
00:15:16,380 --> 00:15:17,670
A reward.

186
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:20,080
Reward?

187
00:15:21,870 --> 00:15:23,110
Yes, Reek.

188
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,680
Those creatures who came in the night,

189
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,800
they wanted to take you away.

190
00:15:28,570 --> 00:15:29,990
And you didn't let them.

191
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:32,930
You remained loyal.

192
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:36,890
I didn't want them to take me.

193
00:15:38,170 --> 00:15:39,430
I was so scared.

194
00:15:39,430 --> 00:15:42,070
-I didn't want them.  -Yes, yes, Reek.

195
00:15:51,370 --> 00:15:52,540
It's a bath.

196
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:54,480
For you.

197
00:15:58,930 --> 00:16:00,370
Remove those rags.

198
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:03,800
Now.

199
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:22,830
The britches, too, Reek.

200
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:24,270
Take them off.

201
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:53,110
Do you love me, Reek?

202
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,650
Yes, of course, my lord.

203
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:04,860
Good.

204
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:07,520
Because I need you to do something for me.

205
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:09,960
Something very important.

206
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:12,560
There's a castle, you see.

207
00:18:13,190 --> 00:18:16,090
Some bad men hold this castle.

208
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:20,190
I need your help to take this castle back.

209
00:18:24,210 --> 00:18:25,190
But how can?

210
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:30,030
I need you to play a role.

211
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:34,230
To pretend to be someone you're not.

212
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:39,690
Pretend to be who?

213
00:18:40,730 --> 00:18:42,780
Theon Greyjoy.

214
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,710
He is a goatherd.

215
00:20:31,050 --> 00:20:34,350
He says he prayed for your victory against the slave masters.

216
00:20:34,870 --> 00:20:36,850
I thank him for his prayers.

217
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:54,880
It was your dragons, he says.

218
00:20:55,250 --> 00:20:57,420
They came this morning for his flock.

219
00:21:01,690 --> 00:21:04,130
He hopes he has not offended Your Grace,

220
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:05,900
but now he has nothing.

221
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:09,450
Tell this man, I am sorry for his hardship.

222
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:11,960
I cannot bring back his goats,

223
00:21:13,050 --> 00:21:17,770
but I will see he is paid their value three times over.

224
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:35,640
Send the next one in.

225
00:22:10,490 --> 00:22:11,700
Queen Daenerys.

226
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:13,950
Tales of your beauty were not exaggerated.

227
00:22:14,930 --> 00:22:15,980
I thank you.

228
00:22:16,010 --> 00:22:19,230
Mine is one of the oldest and proudest families in Meereen.

229
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:21,970
Then it is my honor to receive you.

230
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,890
My father, one of Meereen's most respected

231
00:22:24,890 --> 00:22:27,670
and beloved citizens, oversaw the restoration

232
00:22:27,670 --> 00:22:30,020
and maintenance of its greatest landmarks.

233
00:22:30,220 --> 00:22:31,690
This pyramid included.

234
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:33,780
For that, he has my gratitude.

235
00:22:33,780 --> 00:22:35,650
I should be honored to meet him.

236
00:22:35,670 --> 00:22:36,840
You have, Your Grace.

237
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:38,630
You crucified him.

238
00:22:41,570 --> 00:22:43,130
I pray you'll never live to see

239
00:22:43,130 --> 00:22:45,380
a member of your family treated so cruelly.

240
00:22:45,390 --> 00:22:48,640
Your father crucified innocent children.

241
00:22:48,670 --> 00:22:52,340
My father spoke out against crucifying those children.

242
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:55,630
He decried it as a criminal act, but was overruled.

243
00:22:55,810 --> 00:22:58,770
Is it justice to answer one crime with another?

244
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:01,250
I am sorry you no longer have a father,

245
00:23:01,250 --> 00:23:04,550
but my treatment of the masters was no crime.

246
00:23:05,070 --> 00:23:07,570
You'd be wise to remember that.

247
00:23:08,750 --> 00:23:10,670
What's done is done.

248
00:23:10,940 --> 00:23:13,850
You are the queen and I am a servant of Meereen.

249
00:23:13,850 --> 00:23:17,710
A servant who does not wish to see its traditions eradicated.

250
00:23:18,050 --> 00:23:20,440
And what traditions do you speak of?

251
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:22,520
The tradition of funeral rite.

252
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:24,840
Proper burial in the Temple of the Graces.

253
00:23:25,950 --> 00:23:29,300
My father and 162 noble Meereenese

254
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:31,410
are still nailed to those posts,

255
00:23:31,420 --> 00:23:34,730
carrion for vultures, rotting in the sun.

256
00:23:44,020 --> 00:23:46,840
Your Grace, I ask that you order these men taken down,

257
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:49,210
so that they might receive proper burials.

258
00:23:49,210 --> 00:23:53,210
And what of the slave children these noble Meereenese crucified?

259
00:23:53,590 --> 00:23:55,780
They were rotting in the sun as well.

260
00:23:56,050 --> 00:23:59,320
Would you have begged me for their right to a proper burial?

261
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:02,390
Your Grace, I cannot defend the actions of the masters.

262
00:24:02,390 --> 00:24:06,170
I can only speak to you as a son who loved his father.

263
00:24:06,350 --> 00:24:08,240
Let me take his body down.

264
00:24:09,570 --> 00:24:11,100
Let me have him brought to the temple

265
00:24:11,100 --> 00:24:12,690
and buried with dignity,

266
00:24:12,690 --> 00:24:15,300
so that he might find peace in the next world.

267
00:24:18,900 --> 00:24:22,090
Bury your father, Hizdahr zo Loraq.

268
00:24:26,410 --> 00:24:28,990
Thank you, my queen.

269
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:42,150
How many more?

270
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:45,650
There are 212 supplicants waiting, Your Grace.

271
00:24:45,840 --> 00:24:48,080
212?

272
00:24:56,110 --> 00:24:57,750
Send the next one in.

273
00:25:00,180 --> 00:25:03,030
These meetings aren't always going to be this early, are they?

274
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:05,150
I was up late last night.

275
00:25:06,060 --> 00:25:10,130
So, does this mean I am a master of something now?

276
00:25:10,130 --> 00:25:11,950
Coins, ships?

277
00:25:11,950 --> 00:25:14,390
Lord Tywin and I already determined

278
00:25:14,390 --> 00:25:17,360
that I shall be the Master of Ships long before you.

279
00:25:22,870 --> 00:25:24,430
Lord Tywin, it's a great honor

280
00:25:24,430 --> 00:25:26,840
to have been granted a seat on this council.

281
00:25:26,850 --> 00:25:28,840
The trial begins this afternoon.

282
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:31,210
We only have the morning for affairs of state.

283
00:25:31,220 --> 00:25:32,470
Shall we begin?

284
00:25:32,950 --> 00:25:36,780
Sandor Clegane has been spotted in the Riverlands, my lord.

285
00:25:37,290 --> 00:25:38,870
A coward and a traitor.

286
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:42,820
My birds tell me the Hound slaughtered five of our soldiers.

287
00:25:43,060 --> 00:25:46,040
I believe the phrase "fuck the king" was uttered.

288
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:47,580
Disgraceful.

289
00:25:47,580 --> 00:25:49,440
What would it take to make the common soldier

290
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:51,870
stupid enough to try his luck with the Hound?

291
00:25:51,870 --> 00:25:54,700
10 silver stags seems a generous bounty.

292
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:57,610
Make it 100. What else?

293
00:25:57,770 --> 00:26:00,110
More whispers from the east, my lord.

294
00:26:00,110 --> 00:26:01,640
The Targaryen girl?

295
00:26:01,860 --> 00:26:04,480
Daenerys has taken up residence in Meereen.

296
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:08,030
She has conquered the city and rules as its queen.

297
00:26:08,230 --> 00:26:09,450
Conquered with what?

298
00:26:09,450 --> 00:26:11,680
She commands an army of Unsullied, my queen.

299
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:13,560
Some 8,000 strong.

300
00:26:13,940 --> 00:26:17,450
She has a company of sellswords, the Second Sons.

301
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:19,980
She has two knights advising her.

302
00:26:19,980 --> 00:26:23,400
Jorah Mormont and Barristan Selmy.

303
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:25,470
And she has three dragons.

304
00:26:25,470 --> 00:26:26,780
Baby dragons.

305
00:26:26,780 --> 00:26:29,170
Larger every year, Your Grace.

306
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:32,270
Mormont is spying on her for us.

307
00:26:32,270 --> 00:26:35,420
No longer. He appears to be fully devoted to her.

308
00:26:35,510 --> 00:26:38,560
As for Ser Barristan, it would seem

309
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:42,900
he took his dismissal from the Kingsguard a bit harder than anticipated.

310
00:26:42,980 --> 00:26:44,350
He's an old man.

311
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:46,870
He wasn't fit to protect my son.

312
00:26:46,870 --> 00:26:49,050
Joffrey didn't die on his watch.

313
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:52,420
Dismissing him was as insulting as it was stupid.

314
00:26:52,420 --> 00:26:55,470
Don't tell me you're worried about a child halfway across the world.

315
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:59,010
A child with two seasoned warriors counseling her

316
00:26:59,170 --> 00:27:02,160
and a powerful army at her back, Your Grace.

317
00:27:02,170 --> 00:27:03,360
Lord Varys is right.

318
00:27:03,970 --> 00:27:06,890
I have been to Essos and seen the Unsullied firsthand.

319
00:27:07,270 --> 00:27:09,510
They are very impressive on the battlefield.

320
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:12,160
Less so in the bedroom.

321
00:27:12,160 --> 00:27:14,820
Dragons haven't won a war in 300 years.

322
00:27:14,820 --> 00:27:17,100
Armies win them all the time.

323
00:27:18,310 --> 00:27:20,090
She must be dealt with.

324
00:27:20,370 --> 00:27:21,800
How, my lord?

325
00:27:21,970 --> 00:27:23,370
By force?

326
00:27:23,370 --> 00:27:25,320
Eventually, if it comes to that.

327
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:30,580
Can your little birds find their way into Meereen?

328
00:27:30,830 --> 00:27:32,730
Most certainly, my Lord Hand.

329
00:27:32,930 --> 00:27:35,290
Lord Tyrell, be a good man.

330
00:27:35,290 --> 00:27:37,090
Fetch my quill and paper.

331
00:27:58,520 --> 00:27:59,700
Prince Oberyn.

332
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:02,580
Lord Varys.

333
00:28:03,010 --> 00:28:05,960
Only Varys. I'm not actually a nobleman.

334
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:08,590
No one is under obligation to call me lord.

335
00:28:08,590 --> 00:28:10,390
And yet everyone does.

336
00:28:12,840 --> 00:28:15,350
You seem quite knowledgeable about the Unsullied.

337
00:28:15,350 --> 00:28:17,470
Did you spend much time in Essos?

338
00:28:17,540 --> 00:28:18,850
Five years.

339
00:28:20,210 --> 00:28:21,680
May I ask why?

340
00:28:22,400 --> 00:28:24,450
'Tis a big and beautiful world.

341
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:27,120
Most of us live and die

342
00:28:27,120 --> 00:28:28,830
in the same corner where we were born

343
00:28:28,830 --> 00:28:31,270
and never get to see any of it.

344
00:28:32,530 --> 00:28:34,530
I don't want to be most of us.

345
00:28:34,530 --> 00:28:36,520
Most of us aren't princes.

346
00:28:38,810 --> 00:28:41,420
You are from Essos.

347
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:44,470
Where? Lys?

348
00:28:45,700 --> 00:28:47,250
I have an ear for accents.

349
00:28:47,250 --> 00:28:49,180
I've lost my accent entirely.

350
00:28:49,180 --> 00:28:50,690
I have an ear for that as well.

351
00:28:52,660 --> 00:28:54,350
How did you get here?

352
00:28:54,740 --> 00:28:56,380
It's a long story.

353
00:28:56,590 --> 00:28:58,190
One you don't like telling people.

354
00:29:00,210 --> 00:29:01,740
People I trust.

355
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:05,080
My paramour Ellaria, she would find you very interesting.

356
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:06,800
You should come to the brothel and meet her.

357
00:29:07,270 --> 00:29:10,660
We brought our own wine, not the swill they serve here.

358
00:29:10,750 --> 00:29:13,430
We have some lovely boys on retainer, but.

359
00:29:16,740 --> 00:29:19,100
You did like boys before?

360
00:29:21,280 --> 00:29:22,500
Really?

361
00:29:22,830 --> 00:29:24,390
Girls?

362
00:29:24,980 --> 00:29:25,930
I hope you won't be offended

363
00:29:25,940 --> 00:29:27,640
when I say I never would have guessed.

364
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:29,030
Not at all.

365
00:29:29,110 --> 00:29:32,090
But I was never interested in girls, either.

366
00:29:32,090 --> 00:29:34,380
-What then?  -Nothing.

367
00:29:34,580 --> 00:29:37,150
Everybody is interested in something.

368
00:29:37,150 --> 00:29:38,490
Not me.

369
00:29:38,650 --> 00:29:40,800
When I see what desire does to people,

370
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:42,700
what it's done to this country,

371
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:46,100
I am very glad to have no part in it.

372
00:29:47,140 --> 00:29:50,420
Besides, the absence of desire

373
00:29:50,420 --> 00:29:53,570
leaves one free to pursue other things.

374
00:29:53,570 --> 00:29:54,950
Such as?

375
00:30:30,660 --> 00:30:33,680
Let me guess, I've been pardoned.

376
00:30:50,050 --> 00:30:51,080
Really?

377
00:30:53,190 --> 00:30:54,670
Father's orders.

378
00:30:54,700 --> 00:30:58,380
Well, we mustn't disappoint Father.

379
00:31:08,650 --> 00:31:09,920
Kingslayer!

380
00:31:56,880 --> 00:32:01,620
I, Tommen of the House Baratheon, first of my Name,

381
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:03,730
King of the Andals and the First Men,

382
00:32:04,390 --> 00:32:06,520
and Lord of the Seven Kingdoms,

383
00:32:06,590 --> 00:32:09,800
do hereby recuse myself from this trial.

384
00:32:10,850 --> 00:32:13,520
Tywin of the House Lannister, Hand of the King,

385
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:17,490
Protector of the Realm, will sit as judge in my stead.

386
00:32:18,390 --> 00:32:21,440
And with him Prince Oberyn of the House Martell

387
00:32:21,890 --> 00:32:24,220
and Lord Mace of the House Tyrell.

388
00:32:25,600 --> 00:32:26,910
And if found guilty,

389
00:32:29,230 --> 00:32:31,040
may the gods punish the accused.

390
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:08,810
Tyrion of the House Lannister,

391
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:12,840
you stand accused by the Queen Regent of regicide.

392
00:33:14,710 --> 00:33:16,790
Did you kill King Joffrey?

393
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:19,620
No.

394
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:21,890
Did your wife, the Lady Sansa?

395
00:33:22,520 --> 00:33:24,330
Not that I know of.

396
00:33:24,910 --> 00:33:27,200
How would you say he died, then?

397
00:33:27,710 --> 00:33:29,890
Choked on his pigeon pie.

398
00:33:31,280 --> 00:33:33,300
So you would blame the bakers?

399
00:33:33,300 --> 00:33:36,080
Or the pigeons. Just leave me out of it.

400
00:33:38,810 --> 00:33:41,420
The crown may call its first witness.

401
00:33:41,950 --> 00:33:44,470
Once we'd got King Joffrey safely away from the mob,

402
00:33:44,470 --> 00:33:46,060
the Imp rounded on him.

403
00:33:46,100 --> 00:33:48,130
He slapped the king across the face

404
00:33:48,290 --> 00:33:50,890
and called him a vicious idiot and a fool.

405
00:33:52,370 --> 00:33:54,690
It wasn't the first time the Imp threatened Joffrey.

406
00:33:54,690 --> 00:33:56,460
Right here in this throne room,

407
00:33:56,460 --> 00:33:59,880
he marched up those steps and called our king a halfwit.

408
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:01,580
Compared his Grace to the Mad King

409
00:34:01,580 --> 00:34:03,630
and suggested he'd meet the same fate.

410
00:34:03,630 --> 00:34:05,810
And when I spoke in the king's defense,

411
00:34:05,820 --> 00:34:07,460
he threatened to have me killed.

412
00:34:07,460 --> 00:34:10,230
Oh, why don't you tell them what Joffrey was doing?

413
00:34:10,230 --> 00:34:12,410
-Silence.  -Pointing a loaded crossbow at Sansa Stark

414
00:34:12,410 --> 00:34:14,330
while you tore at her clothes and beat her.

415
00:34:14,330 --> 00:34:15,670
Silence!

416
00:34:17,850 --> 00:34:20,700
You will not speak unless called upon.

417
00:34:22,570 --> 00:34:24,100
You're dismissed, Ser Meryn.

418
00:34:31,450 --> 00:34:33,530
Basilisk venom,

419
00:34:34,020 --> 00:34:35,720
widow's blood,

420
00:34:36,530 --> 00:34:38,040
wolfsbane,

421
00:34:38,360 --> 00:34:40,750
essence of nightshade,

422
00:34:41,180 --> 00:34:42,720
sweetsleep,

423
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:45,220
tears of Lys,

424
00:34:45,880 --> 00:34:47,600
demon's dance,

425
00:34:50,500 --> 00:34:51,510
blindeye.

426
00:34:51,510 --> 00:34:53,900
I think you have made your point, Grand Maester.

427
00:34:53,900 --> 00:34:55,820
You have a lot of poison in your store.

428
00:34:55,820 --> 00:34:58,010
Had, Prince Oberyn.

429
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:00,840
My stores were plundered.

430
00:35:00,840 --> 00:35:01,990
By whom?

431
00:35:02,380 --> 00:35:04,860
By the accused, Tyrion Lannister,

432
00:35:04,860 --> 00:35:07,640
after he had me wrongfully imprisoned.

433
00:35:07,650 --> 00:35:09,140
Grand Maester,

434
00:35:10,040 --> 00:35:13,030
you examined King Joffrey's corpse.

435
00:35:13,740 --> 00:35:17,230
Was it without question poison that killed him?

436
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:19,740
Without question.

437
00:35:22,380 --> 00:35:24,390
This was found on the body of

438
00:35:24,390 --> 00:35:26,960
Dontos Hollard, the king's fool.

439
00:35:27,300 --> 00:35:31,450
He was last seen spiriting Sansa Stark,

440
00:35:31,450 --> 00:35:35,040
the wife of the accused, away from the feast.

441
00:35:35,600 --> 00:35:38,980
She wore this necklace,

442
00:35:38,980 --> 00:35:40,380
the day of the wedding.

443
00:35:41,550 --> 00:35:44,140
Residue of a most rare

444
00:35:44,140 --> 00:35:48,400
and terrible poison was found inside.

445
00:35:49,340 --> 00:35:52,250
Was this one of the poisons stolen from your store?

446
00:35:52,260 --> 00:35:55,230
It was. The Strangler.

447
00:35:56,130 --> 00:35:59,470
A poison few in the Seven Kingdoms possess.

448
00:36:00,210 --> 00:36:03,600
And used to strike down the most noble child

449
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:06,870
the gods ever put on this good earth.

450
00:36:14,770 --> 00:36:16,540
"I will hurt you for this.

451
00:36:16,640 --> 00:36:19,720
A day will come when you think you are safe and happy

452
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:22,450
and your joy will turn to ashes in your mouth

453
00:36:22,450 --> 00:36:24,630
and you will know the debt is paid."

454
00:36:25,690 --> 00:36:28,130
Your own brother said this to you?

455
00:36:29,670 --> 00:36:32,210
Shortly before the Battle of Blackwater Bay.

456
00:36:32,570 --> 00:36:34,610
I confronted him about his plans

457
00:36:34,610 --> 00:36:36,510
to put Joffrey on the front lines.

458
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:40,780
As it turned out, when the attack came,

459
00:36:40,780 --> 00:36:43,300
Joff insisted on remaining at the battlements.

460
00:36:43,300 --> 00:36:47,110
He believed his presence would inspire the troops.

461
00:36:48,820 --> 00:36:50,070
Tyrion said,

462
00:36:50,670 --> 00:36:53,350
"And you will know the debt is paid."

463
00:36:54,010 --> 00:36:55,440
What debt?

464
00:36:56,360 --> 00:36:57,990
I discovered he'd been keeping whores

465
00:36:57,990 --> 00:36:59,740
in the Tower of the Hand.

466
00:36:59,760 --> 00:37:02,610
I asked him to confine his salacious acts

467
00:37:02,610 --> 00:37:05,300
to the brothel where such behavior belongs.

468
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:07,400
He wasn't pleased.

469
00:37:10,020 --> 00:37:14,000
Thank you, Your Grace, for the courage of your testimony.

470
00:37:30,130 --> 00:37:32,720
Do you remember the precise nature of this threat?

471
00:37:33,330 --> 00:37:35,200
I'm afraid I do, my lord.

472
00:37:35,410 --> 00:37:38,750
He said, "Perhaps you should speak more softly to me, then.

473
00:37:38,940 --> 00:37:40,650
Monsters are dangerous

474
00:37:40,750 --> 00:37:43,600
and just now kings are dying like flies."

475
00:37:43,640 --> 00:37:46,660
And he said this to you at a meeting of the small council?

476
00:37:46,660 --> 00:37:47,730
Yes.

477
00:37:48,080 --> 00:37:51,110
After we received word of Robb Stark's death.

478
00:37:51,110 --> 00:37:53,590
He didn't seem gladdened by the news.

479
00:37:53,620 --> 00:37:55,880
Perhaps his marriage to Sansa Stark

480
00:37:55,880 --> 00:37:58,680
had made him more sympathetic to the northern cause.

481
00:38:02,660 --> 00:38:04,610
You're excused, Lord Varys.

482
00:38:06,400 --> 00:38:09,770
Father, may I ask the witness one question?

483
00:38:16,250 --> 00:38:17,350
One.

484
00:38:21,180 --> 00:38:22,350
You once said,

485
00:38:22,850 --> 00:38:26,220
that without me, this city would have faced certain defeat.

486
00:38:26,490 --> 00:38:30,190
You said the histories would never mention me,

487
00:38:30,740 --> 00:38:32,780
but you would not forget.

488
00:38:34,480 --> 00:38:37,060
Have you forgotten, Lord Varys?

489
00:38:39,720 --> 00:38:41,480
Sadly, my lord,

490
00:38:42,100 --> 00:38:43,970
I never forget a thing.

491
00:38:54,360 --> 00:38:55,980
We will adjourn for now.

492
00:38:57,850 --> 00:38:59,960
Toll the bells in an hour's time.

493
00:39:00,170 --> 00:39:01,640
Clear the court!

494
00:39:22,780 --> 00:39:24,660
You'd condemn your own son to death?

495
00:39:24,660 --> 00:39:27,090
I've condemned no one. The trial is not over.

496
00:39:27,170 --> 00:39:28,730
This isn't a trial. It's a farce.

497
00:39:28,730 --> 00:39:30,860
Cersei has manipulated everything and you know it.

498
00:39:30,950 --> 00:39:32,340
I know nothing of the sort.

499
00:39:32,340 --> 00:39:34,750
-You've always hated Tyrion.  -He killed his king.

500
00:39:34,750 --> 00:39:35,810
As did I.

501
00:39:37,080 --> 00:39:39,140
Do you know the last order the Mad King gave me?

502
00:39:39,550 --> 00:39:41,010
To bring him your head.

503
00:39:42,540 --> 00:39:44,890
I saved your life, so you could murder my brother?

504
00:39:44,890 --> 00:39:47,150
-It won't be murder. It'll be justice.  -Justice?

505
00:39:47,830 --> 00:39:50,830
I'm performing my sworn duty as Hand of the King.

506
00:39:50,840 --> 00:39:53,570
If Tyrion is found guilty, he will be punished accordingly.

507
00:39:53,570 --> 00:39:55,930
-He'll be executed.  -No, he'll be punished accordingly.

508
00:39:59,150 --> 00:40:03,650
Once you said, family is what lives on. All that lives on.

509
00:40:04,130 --> 00:40:07,310
You told me about a dynasty that would last 1,000 years.

510
00:40:07,720 --> 00:40:09,930
What happens to your dynasty when Tyrion dies?

511
00:40:11,980 --> 00:40:12,980
I'm a Kingsguard,

512
00:40:13,400 --> 00:40:15,460
forbidden by oath to carry on the family line.

513
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:16,910
I'm well aware of your oath.

514
00:40:16,910 --> 00:40:18,580
What happens to your name?

515
00:40:19,640 --> 00:40:21,980
Who carries the lion banner into future battles?

516
00:40:22,980 --> 00:40:23,820
Your nephews?

517
00:40:24,780 --> 00:40:26,070
Lancel Lannister?

518
00:40:26,720 --> 00:40:28,510
Others whose names I don't even remember?

519
00:40:28,520 --> 00:40:29,940
What happens to my dynasty

520
00:40:29,940 --> 00:40:32,470
if I spare the life of my grandson's killer?

521
00:40:32,670 --> 00:40:34,700
It survives through me.

522
00:40:37,810 --> 00:40:39,050
I'll leave the Kingsguard.

523
00:40:40,190 --> 00:40:43,190
I'll take my place as your son and heir

524
00:40:43,190 --> 00:40:45,010
if you let Tyrion live.

525
00:40:45,260 --> 00:40:45,900
Done.

526
00:40:48,750 --> 00:40:51,600
When the testimony's concluded and a guilty verdict rendered,

527
00:40:51,600 --> 00:40:53,610
Tyrion will be given the chance to speak.

528
00:40:53,610 --> 00:40:57,290
He'll plead for mercy. I'll allow him to join the Night's Watch.

529
00:40:59,730 --> 00:41:01,970
In three days' time, he'll depart for Castle Black

530
00:41:01,970 --> 00:41:03,710
and live out his days at the Wall.

531
00:41:03,810 --> 00:41:06,170
You'll remove your white cloak immediately.

532
00:41:06,880 --> 00:41:08,310
You will leave King's Landing

533
00:41:08,320 --> 00:41:10,770
to assume your rightful place at Casterly Rock.

534
00:41:11,610 --> 00:41:13,120
You will marry a suitable woman

535
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:16,130
and father children named Lannister.

536
00:41:16,630 --> 00:41:19,740
And you'll never turn your back on your family again.

537
00:41:25,740 --> 00:41:26,750
You have my word.

538
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:28,230
And you have mine.

539
00:41:53,450 --> 00:41:55,040
Not going well, is it?

540
00:41:55,040 --> 00:41:57,290
-You're going to be found guilty.  -Oh, you think so?

541
00:41:57,290 --> 00:42:00,140
When you are, you need to enter a formal plea for mercy

542
00:42:00,150 --> 00:42:01,510
and ask to be sent to the Wall.

543
00:42:02,830 --> 00:42:04,010
Father's agreed to it.

544
00:42:04,810 --> 00:42:07,140
He'll spare your life and allow you to join the Night's Watch.

545
00:42:08,210 --> 00:42:10,130
Ned Stark was promised the same thing

546
00:42:10,130 --> 00:42:11,690
and we both know how that turned out.

547
00:42:11,690 --> 00:42:13,960
Father is not Joffrey. He'll keep his word.

548
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:14,920
How do you know?

549
00:42:19,860 --> 00:42:20,710
Do you trust me?

550
00:42:24,900 --> 00:42:26,880
Keep your mouth shut. No more outbursts.

551
00:42:27,660 --> 00:42:28,880
This will all be over soon.

552
00:42:45,610 --> 00:42:47,820
The crown may call its next witness.

553
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:23,910
State your name.

554
00:43:25,980 --> 00:43:26,700
Shae.

555
00:43:27,300 --> 00:43:28,580
Do you swear by all the gods

556
00:43:28,580 --> 00:43:31,110
that your testimony will be true and honest?

557
00:43:32,830 --> 00:43:33,720
I swear it.

558
00:43:34,530 --> 00:43:35,530
Do you know this man?

559
00:43:44,230 --> 00:43:46,440
Yes. Tyrion Lannister.

560
00:43:47,440 --> 00:43:48,570
How do you know him?

561
00:43:48,900 --> 00:43:51,760
I was handmaiden to his wife Lady Sansa.

562
00:43:52,520 --> 00:43:55,820
This man stands accused of murdering King Joffrey.

563
00:43:56,950 --> 00:43:58,410
What do you know of this?

564
00:44:00,500 --> 00:44:02,040
I know that he's guilty.

565
00:44:03,900 --> 00:44:05,670
He and Sansa planned it together.

566
00:44:06,910 --> 00:44:07,610
Silence!

567
00:44:10,670 --> 00:44:11,310
Continue.

568
00:44:12,480 --> 00:44:16,290
She wanted revenge for her father, her mother, her brother.

569
00:44:16,530 --> 00:44:18,410
She blamed their deaths on the king.

570
00:44:19,510 --> 00:44:21,030
Tyrion was happy to help.

571
00:44:22,330 --> 00:44:25,070
He hated Joffrey. He hated the queen.

572
00:44:26,130 --> 00:44:27,410
He hated you, my lord.

573
00:44:29,340 --> 00:44:31,640
He stole poison from the Grand Maester's chamber

574
00:44:31,650 --> 00:44:33,180
to put in Joffrey's wine.

575
00:44:33,840 --> 00:44:35,650
How could you possibly know all this?

576
00:44:36,320 --> 00:44:39,750
Why would he reveal such plans to his wife's maid?

577
00:44:41,930 --> 00:44:43,290
I wasn't just her maid.

578
00:44:47,360 --> 00:44:48,410
I was his whore.

579
00:44:49,730 --> 00:44:50,830
I beg your pardon?

580
00:44:51,220 --> 00:44:52,670
You said you were his.

581
00:44:53,840 --> 00:44:54,980
His whore.

582
00:44:57,930 --> 00:45:00,200
How did you come to be in his service?

583
00:45:00,340 --> 00:45:01,270
He stole me.

584
00:45:01,890 --> 00:45:04,650
I was with another man, a knight in your lordship's army.

585
00:45:05,100 --> 00:45:06,980
But when Tyrion arrived at the camp,

586
00:45:07,400 --> 00:45:09,780
he sent one of his cutthroats into our tent.

587
00:45:10,800 --> 00:45:12,190
He broke the knight's arm

588
00:45:12,190 --> 00:45:13,720
and brought me to Lord Tyrion.

589
00:45:14,500 --> 00:45:16,190
"You belong to me now," he said.

590
00:45:17,280 --> 00:45:18,430
"I want you to fuck me

591
00:45:18,430 --> 00:45:20,440
like it's my last night in this world."

592
00:45:23,990 --> 00:45:25,960
Silence. Silence!

593
00:45:27,750 --> 00:45:28,790
And did you?

594
00:45:30,170 --> 00:45:30,950
Did I what?

595
00:45:31,840 --> 00:45:34,300
Fuck him like it was his last night in this world.

596
00:45:36,710 --> 00:45:38,450
I did everything he wanted.

597
00:45:39,110 --> 00:45:41,090
Whatever he told me to do to him.

598
00:45:41,160 --> 00:45:42,890
Whatever he felt like doing to me.

599
00:45:43,550 --> 00:45:45,080
I kissed him where he wanted.

600
00:45:45,090 --> 00:45:46,560
I licked him where he wanted.

601
00:45:46,690 --> 00:45:49,570
I let him put himself where he wanted.

602
00:45:50,210 --> 00:45:51,470
I was his property.

603
00:45:51,990 --> 00:45:53,970
I would wait in his chambers for hours,

604
00:45:53,970 --> 00:45:55,750
so he could use me when he was bored.

605
00:45:57,030 --> 00:45:59,730
He ordered me to call him "my lion," so I did.

606
00:46:01,350 --> 00:46:03,480
I took his face in my hands and said,

607
00:46:04,460 --> 00:46:06,400
"I am yours and you are mine."

608
00:46:11,210 --> 00:46:11,960
Shae.

609
00:46:15,680 --> 00:46:16,530
Please don't.

610
00:46:20,630 --> 00:46:21,710
I am a whore.

611
00:46:22,920 --> 00:46:23,560
Remember?

612
00:46:26,460 --> 00:46:28,280
That was before he married Sansa.

613
00:46:28,890 --> 00:46:31,020
After that, all he wanted was her.

614
00:46:31,950 --> 00:46:33,680
But she wouldn't let him into her bed.

615
00:46:35,200 --> 00:46:37,560
So he promised to kill King Joffrey for her.

616
00:46:47,720 --> 00:46:48,490
Father.

617
00:46:49,950 --> 00:46:51,220
I wish to confess.

618
00:46:53,530 --> 00:46:55,990
I wish to confess.

619
00:46:58,620 --> 00:47:00,350
You wish to confess?

620
00:47:03,150 --> 00:47:04,090
I saved you.

621
00:47:06,220 --> 00:47:07,520
I saved this city

622
00:47:08,950 --> 00:47:11,360
and all your worthless lives.

623
00:47:12,890 --> 00:47:15,590
I should have let Stannis kill you all.

624
00:47:16,830 --> 00:47:17,650
Tyrion.

625
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:23,390
Do you wish to confess?

626
00:47:27,490 --> 00:47:29,550
Yes, Father.

627
00:47:30,330 --> 00:47:31,270
I'm guilty.

628
00:47:32,370 --> 00:47:35,170
Guilty. Is that what you want to hear?

629
00:47:35,500 --> 00:47:37,350
You admit you poisoned the king?

630
00:47:37,350 --> 00:47:39,960
No, of that I'm innocent.

631
00:47:40,600 --> 00:47:43,880
I'm guilty of a far more monstrous crime.

632
00:47:44,470 --> 00:47:47,500
I am guilty of being a dwarf.

633
00:47:48,770 --> 00:47:51,210
You are not on trial for being a dwarf.

634
00:47:51,210 --> 00:47:53,200
Oh, yes, I am.

635
00:47:53,860 --> 00:47:57,730
I've been on trial for that my entire life.

636
00:47:58,720 --> 00:48:00,590
Have you nothing to say in your defense?

637
00:48:00,590 --> 00:48:01,780
Nothing, but this.

638
00:48:02,840 --> 00:48:04,020
I did not do it.

639
00:48:05,310 --> 00:48:07,680
I did not kill Joffrey,

640
00:48:07,840 --> 00:48:10,400
but I wish that I had.

641
00:48:10,470 --> 00:48:13,000
Watching your vicious bastard die

642
00:48:13,100 --> 00:48:17,370
gave me more relief than 1,000 lying whores.

643
00:48:20,660 --> 00:48:24,700
I wish I was the monster you think I am.

644
00:48:25,980 --> 00:48:29,730
I wish I had enough poison for the whole pack of you.

645
00:48:29,780 --> 00:48:34,410
I would gladly give my life to watch you all swallow it.

646
00:48:34,530 --> 00:48:36,080
Ser Meryn. Ser Meryn.

647
00:48:36,270 --> 00:48:38,650
Escort the prisoner back to his cell.

648
00:48:40,610 --> 00:48:45,140
I will not give my life for Joffrey's murder.

649
00:48:45,170 --> 00:48:47,850
And I know I'll get no justice here.

650
00:48:48,010 --> 00:48:51,170
So I will let the gods decide my fate.

651
00:48:53,060 --> 00:48:56,040
I demand a trial by combat.

